    "padding": "labelled call plus margin, centred in zero-valued padding",
    "channel_indices": "every channel the recording carries",
    "channel_policy": "The archive is not uniformly four-channel: read from the fmt chunk of all 81 recordings, 55 carry four channels, 25 carry six and one carries two, all at 48 kHz. That matches the published design of up to three recording units with two microphones each, with a different number of units deployed on different days. Every channel a recording carries is cut. Channels 0 and 1 exist on all 81 recordings, so the paired-channel test on that pair runs corpus-wide; tests involving channels 2 to 5 run on the subset that has them. Channel index is therefore not a stable physical microphone across recordings, and the channel axis is partly confounded with date because unit count changed over time. That is recorded here rather than discovered later.",
    "identity_channel_rule": "the channel with the smallest share of energy below 50 Hz over the annotated call windows of the enrolment split only, chosen among channels 0 and 1 so that one rule applies to every recording"
